{"text":"kuruntokai","n":102,"lines":["உள்ளின் உள்ளம் வேமே உள்ளா","திருப்பினெம் அளவைத் தன்றே வருத்தி","வான்றோய் வற்றே காமம்","சான்றோர் அல்லர்யாம் மரீஇ யோரே"],"tr":["uḷḷiṉ uḷḷam vēmē uḷḷā","tiruppiṉem aḷavait taṉṟē varutti","vāṉṟōy vaṟṟē kāmam","cāṉṟōr allaryām marīi yōrē"],"colophon":{"tinai":"neytal","tinai_ta":"நெய்தல்","speaker_ta":"தலைவி கூற்று","poet_ta":"ஔவையார்","speaker_en":"the heroine (talaivi)","poet_tr":"Auvaiyār"},"scan":{"meter":"nēricai āciriyappā","ok":true,"checks":[{"name":"lines","ok":true,"detail":"4 lines"},{"name":"feet per line","ok":true,"detail":"3×4, 1×3 feet"},{"name":"foot types","ok":true,"detail":"iyaṟcīr 14, veṇcīr 1"},{"name":"linkage","ok":true,"detail":"āciriyattaḷai 11, veṇṭaḷai 2, kalittaḷai 1"},{"name":"ending","ok":true,"detail":"ends on ஏ"}],"ending":"ஏ","lines":[[{"text":"உள்ளின்","tr":"uḷḷiṉ","foot":"tēmā","acai":[{"kind":"nēr","text":"உள்","tr":"uḷ"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"ளின்","tr":"ḷiṉ"}]},{"text":"உள்ளம்","tr":"uḷḷam","foot":"tēmā","acai":[{"kind":"nēr","text":"உள்","tr":"uḷ"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"ளம்","tr":"ḷam"}]},{"text":"வேமே","tr":"vēmē","foot":"tēmā","acai":[{"kind":"nēr","text":"வே","tr":"vē"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"மே","tr":"mē"}]},{"text":"உள்ளா","tr":"uḷḷā","foot":"tēmā","acai":[{"kind":"nēr","text":"உள்","tr":"uḷ"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"ளா","tr":"ḷā"}]}],[{"text":"திருப்பினெம்","tr":"tiruppiṉem","foot":"karuviḷam","acai":[{"kind":"nirai","text":"திருப்","tr":"tirup"},{"kind":"nirai","text":"பினெம்","tr":"piṉem"}]},{"text":"அளவைத்","tr":"aḷavait","foot":"puḷimā","acai":[{"kind":"nirai","text":"அள","tr":"aḷa"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"வைத்","tr":"vait"}]},{"text":"தன்றே","tr":"taṉṟē","foot":"tēmā","acai":[{"kind":"nēr","text":"தன்","tr":"taṉ"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"றே","tr":"ṟē"}]},{"text":"வருத்தி","tr":"varutti","foot":"puḷimā","acai":[{"kind":"nirai","text":"வருத்","tr":"varut"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"தி","tr":"ti"}]}],[{"text":"வான்றோய்","tr":"vāṉṟōy","foot":"tēmā","acai":[{"kind":"nēr","text":"வான்","tr":"vāṉ"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"றோய்","tr":"ṟōy"}]},{"text":"வற்றே","tr":"vaṟṟē","foot":"tēmā","acai":[{"kind":"nēr","text":"வற்","tr":"vaṟ"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"றே","tr":"ṟē"}]},{"text":"காமம்","tr":"kāmam","foot":"tēmā","acai":[{"kind":"nēr","text":"கா","tr":"kā"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"மம்","tr":"mam"}]}],[{"text":"சான்றோர்","tr":"cāṉṟōr","foot":"tēmā","acai":[{"kind":"nēr","text":"சான்","tr":"cāṉ"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"றோர்","tr":"ṟōr"}]},{"text":"அல்லர்யாம்","tr":"allaryām","foot":"tēmāṅkāy","acai":[{"kind":"nēr","text":"அல்","tr":"al"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"லர்","tr":"lar"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"யாம்","tr":"yām"}]},{"text":"மரீஇ","tr":"marīi","foot":"puḷimā","acai":[{"kind":"nirai","text":"மரீ","tr":"marī"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"இ","tr":"i"}]},{"text":"யோரே","tr":"yōrē","foot":"tēmā","acai":[{"kind":"nēr","text":"யோ","tr":"yō"},{"kind":"nēr","text":"ரே","tr":"rē"}]}]]},"ai":{"lines":[{"words":[{"surface":"உள்ளின்","parts":[{"text":"உள்","lemma":"உள்ளு","gloss":"think"},{"text":"இன்","lemma":"இன்","gloss":"if"}],"gloss":"if I think of him"},{"surface":"உள்ளம்","parts":[{"text":"உள்ளம்","lemma":"உள்ளம்","gloss":"heart"}],"gloss":"my heart"},{"surface":"வேமே","parts":[{"text":"வேம்","lemma":"வே","gloss":"burns"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"indeed"}],"gloss":"burns indeed"},{"surface":"உள்ளா","parts":[{"text":"உள்","lemma":"உள்ளு","gloss":"think"},{"text":"ஆ","lemma":"ஆ","gloss":"not"}],"gloss":"without thinking"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"திருப்பின்","parts":[{"text":"திருப்பு","lemma":"திருப்பு","gloss":"turn back"},{"text":"இன்","lemma":"இன்","gloss":"if"}],"gloss":"if turning back"},{"surface":"எம்","parts":[{"text":"எம்","lemma":"யாம்","gloss":"our"}],"gloss":"our"},{"surface":"அளவை","parts":[{"text":"அளவை","lemma":"அளவை","gloss":"measure"}],"gloss":"limit"},{"surface":"தன்று","parts":[{"text":"தன்று","lemma":"அன்று","gloss":"is not"}],"gloss":"is not"},{"surface":"ஏ","parts":[{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"indeed"}],"gloss":"indeed"},{"surface":"வருத்தி","parts":[{"text":"வருத்து","lemma":"வருத்து","gloss":"cause pain"},{"text":"இ","lemma":"இ","gloss":"having"}],"gloss":"causing pain"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"வான்றோய்","parts":[{"text":"வான்றோய்","lemma":"வான்றோய்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"வற்றே","parts":[{"text":"வற்றே","lemma":"வற்றே","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"காமம்","parts":[{"text":"காமம்","lemma":"காமம்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true}],"as_printed":true},{"words":[{"surface":"சான்றோர்","parts":[{"text":"சான்றோர்","lemma":"சான்றோர்","gloss":"noble person"}],"gloss":"noble person","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"அல்லர்","parts":[{"text":"அல்","lemma":"அல்","gloss":"not"},{"text":"அர்","lemma":"அர்","gloss":"he"}],"gloss":"he is not"},{"surface":"யாம்","parts":[{"text":"யாம்","lemma":"யாம்","gloss":"we"}],"gloss":"I"},{"surface":"மரீஇயோரே","parts":[{"text":"மரீஇயோரே","lemma":"மரீஇயோரே","gloss":"the one whom I associated with indeed"}],"gloss":"the one whom I associated with indeed","split_unverified":true}]}],"literal":"If I think, my heart burns indeed; without thinking, / if we turn it back, it is indeed not within our limit, causing pain, / touching the sky is of such nature, love; / a noble person he is not, the one whom I associated with.","translation":"If I think of him, my heart burns. If I try not to think of him and turn my mind back, it is beyond my power, and it only tortures me. My love is as vast as the sky it touches. He is indeed not a noble man, the one with whom I united.","modern":"அவரை நினைத்தால் என் நெஞ்சம் எரிகிறது. நினைக்காமல் மனதைத் திருப்ப முயன்றால், அது என் கட்டுப்பாட்டுக்குள் இல்லை; அது என்னை வருத்துகிறது. என் காதல் வானத்தைத் தொடும் அளவுக்குப் பெரியது. நான் நெருங்கிப் பழகிய அவர் சான்றோர் அல்லர்.","explanation":"The heroine is speaking to her close friend about her uncontrollable grief during separation. She explains that she is caught in a painful dilemma: thinking of her lover burns her heart, but trying to turn her mind away from him is impossible as it exceeds her mental strength and only causes further distress. She describes her love as something so immense that it touches the sky. She laments that the man she intimately associated with is not a noble person, because he has left her to suffer in this manner. This poem belongs to the Neytal tiṇai (seashore landscape), which traditionally represents the themes of waiting, anxiety, and lamentation in love.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"}}